Exercises
==================================================

Project: Project SEKAI / Vocaloid Song Library

Instructions:

Create the React components in separate files.

You may choose the songs and fill in the information yourself.

Each song should contain:

- id
- song
- artist
- vocals
- unit
- difficulty
- vocaloid

Note: Vocals may also contain a Vocaloid. This is okay.


1. Create a Song List

   Create a song list in App.jsx containing at least 5 songs.

   Each song should have:

   - id
   - song
   - artist
   - vocals
   - unit
   - difficulty
   - vocaloid

   You may choose the songs yourself.


2. Create SongList.jsx

   Create a separate SongList.jsx component.

   App.jsx should pass the song list to SongList using props.

   SongList should receive the songs and display them.


3. Create SongCard.jsx

   Create a separate SongCard.jsx component.

   SongList should use .map() to create a SongCard for every song.

   Pass the song information from SongList to SongCard using props.

   SongCard should display:

   - Song
   - Artist
   - Vocals
   - Unit
   - Difficulty
   - Vocaloid


4. Add More Songs

   Continue using the same component files:

   App.jsx
   SongList.jsx
   SongCard.jsx

   Add at least 5 more songs to the existing song array.

   You should now have at least 10 songs in total.

   Do NOT create a new component for each song.

   Use the same SongCard component for every song.

   Make sure every song has a unique id.

   Use the song's id as the key when using .map().


5. Create Card.jsx

   Create a new reusable Card.jsx component.

   Use props.children so that other components can place their
   content inside the Card.

   Change SongCard so that its song information is displayed
   inside the reusable Card component.


6. Add Song Selection

   Add a "Select" button to every SongCard.

   Create a callback prop that allows SongCard to tell the parent
   which song was selected.

   Do not store the selected song inside SongCard.


7. Store the Selected Song

   Store the selected song in App.jsx using useState.

   When the user clicks a SongCard's Select button, update the
   selected song.

   Create a SongDetails.jsx component.

   Pass the selected song from App.jsx to SongDetails using props.


8. Use Conditional Rendering

   Use conditional rendering in SongDetails.

   If no song has been selected, display:

   "Please select a song."

   If a song has been selected, display its information.


9. Add Difficulty Filtering

   Add a difficulty filter.

   The user should be able to select a difficulty such as:

   All
   Easy
   Normal
   Hard
   Expert
   Master

   Only display songs that match the selected difficulty.

   Keep the main song data in App.jsx.

   Use the necessary state, props, and components to control
   the filter.


10. Add Unit Filtering

    Add a unit filter and finish the Song Library.

    The user should be able to select a unit.

    Only display songs belonging to the selected unit.

    The final project should include:

    - At least 10 songs
    - Separate component files
    - Props
    - props.children
    - Callback props
    - Lifting state up
    - Conditional rendering
    - Lists and keys
    - Song selection
    - Difficulty filtering
    - Unit filtering

    Suggested component structure:

    App.jsx
    ├── SongList.jsx
    │   └── SongCard.jsx
    │       └── Card.jsx
    └── SongDetails.jsx

    You may add more components if you think they are useful.
